Genera of fungi that cause ringworm (any two):
- **Microsporum**;
- **Trichophyton**;
- **Epidermophyton**.

Symptoms (any two):
- appearance of **dry, scaly lesions** on various parts of the body, such as the skin, nails and scalp;
- the lesions are accompanied by **intense itching**.

Heat and moisture help these fungi grow, so ringworm is common in skin folds such as the groin or between the toes.

